# Neo Learn Granular parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.5). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnGranular
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnGrain
class NeoLearnGranularMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching granular synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A source recording (Dye's five built-in samples, or your own WAV) cut into short windowed grains read around a frozen scan position, with grain size, density, spray, a pitch shimmer (micro-pitch wander and octave-up grains) and a grain contour that morphs the window from trapezoid to Gaussian, an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for ambient clouds, frozen textures, glitchy stutters and shimmering pads, or to learn how granular synthesis works.
import sample .wav | A WAV sample (mono or stereo, up to 20 s, kept in the machine state): the source the grains are cut from. Item 0. The source can also be one of the built-in samples (kind "source": Choir, Strings, Bell, Pluck or Texture).

group Core
SamplePosition   "Scan Position" 0 1000 300 pct
    id sample_position
    how Moves the center playhead location from which audio grains are extracted in the source recording.
    sound Scrubs through different timbral moments of the source audio as if freezing time at that spot.
GrainSize        "Grain Size" 0 1000 690 time 0.005 0.5
    id grain_size
    how Sets the duration of each individual audio slice extracted from the buffer.
    sound Very short grains (< 25 ms) sound buzzy and robotic; long grains (> 150 ms) create smooth, lush ambient clouds.
GrainDensity     "Density" 0 1000 720 exp 1 64 grains/s 1
    id grain_density
    how Controls how many new grains are triggered per second per active voice.
    sound Low density produces sparse, stuttering rhythmic droplets; high density fuses grains into a continuous pad. At most 10 grains overlap per note; beyond that the oldest fade out.
PositionSpray    "Time Spray" 0 1000 200 pct
    id position_spray
    how Randomizes each grain's start offset around the main sample_position playhead.
    sound Eliminates repetitive looping buzz and smears the recording into an organic, non-repeating texture.
PitchShimmer     "Pitch Shimmer" 0 1000 0 pct
    id pitch_shimmer
    how Introduces micro-pitch randomization (up to 25 cents either way) and gradually adds grains pitched +12 semitones (one octave up, up to half of them at 100%).
    sound Adds a crystalline, angelic octave glow above ambient pads.
GrainShape       "Grain Contour" 0 1000 700 pct
    id grain_shape
    how Morphs the amplitude window of each grain from sharp trapezoid edges (0%) to smooth Gaussian curves (100%).
    sound Low values sound clicky and glitchy; high values crossfade grains seamlessly without rhythmic transients.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 551 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 718 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 1000 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 630 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 604 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnGranularMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
